WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.570
Point a detector at a decaying source
and record the corrected count rate,

2
00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:06.350
again and again.

3
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:10.880
Plot it against time, and you get a
curve that falls more and more slowly.

4
00:00:10.930 --> 00:00:14.260
And because decay is
random, the points scatter.

5
00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:17.660
Pick any two of them, and
your half-life wobbles.

6
00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:22.270
So how can a straight line reveal
a half-life hidden inside a curve?

7
00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:25.380
In this mission, you'll make
that falling curve straight,

8
00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:27.750
and find out what the line tells you.

9
00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:30.700
Then you'll read a half-life
from a best-fit line,

10
00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:33.320
so the random scatter averages out.

11
00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:37.640
Your mission: find the half-life of
a source from a straight-line graph.
